    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d129">

                <pb facs="0280" n="188" xml:id="pg188"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/9614</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador on Special Mission</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Reading</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 353</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 2, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have just received a
                    telegram from the Prime Minister asking me to convey to the President the
                    sincere thanks of the War Cabinet for his instant and complete response to the
                    appeal of the British and French Governments.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d129-f1"/> It
                    has come as the greatest relief to all those who have the immediate
                    responsibility for dealing with this crisis to know that, thanks to the
                    President’s prompt co-operation, the Allied armies are to receive an
                    indispensable reinforcement of men during the next few vital months.</p>
                <p>May I ask you to be good enough to convey to the President the above message from
                    Mr. Lloyd George.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d129-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reading</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d129-f1" n="1" xml:id="d129-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram transmitted by the Adjutant General, Mar. 29, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg187">p. 187</ref>. Response
                    was also made orally by the President to the British Ambassador.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d129-f2" n="2" xml:id="d129-f2-content">
                <p>Shown to the President, Apr. 2.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
